  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nThe broad trough will remain in place through the weekend and\ninto next week, with temperatures returning to seasonal values \nfor early October. The cooler temperatures will be reinforced by\na shortwave digging through the upper trough on Sunday. This \nwave could pull moisture, from the boundary that becomes diffuse\nto the south of our region after crossing today, northward, \nleading to some possible showers south and east of Pittsburgh. \nAt this time the probability of more than a few light \nshowers/sprinkles is fairly low (Prob > 0.05 inches around 30% \nin the WV ridges). At this point, the ridges are mainly an\nslight assist in lift through the day on Sunday. After Sunday, \nbuilding surface high pressure looks to keep the region dry for \nmuch of the rest of the week. \n\nWith the passage of the front finally on Sunday, the core of the\ncolder moving in behind that will be cold enough for a frost\npotential on Monday night and Tuesday night. This probability\nwill mainly be east and northeast of Pittsburgh. The NBM still,\ngives a good >50% prob for the frost. Otherwise, a dry forecast\npersists.",
